[2m > {"session_id":"Fdwg1GRL0jFMSqRt","results":[{"source_id":"t70FeA2l_IIEnnMUVIHmP","url":"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8590148-memory-in-chatgpt","title":"Memory in ChatGPT","publish_date":null,"excerpts":["Don't mention this again reduces future references to the information. It does not delete the original source.\n\n**Delete and turn off memory** deletes the remembered information shown in the summary and turns **Memory** off. It does not delete past chats.\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.58.35 AM\n\n## Sources\n\nWhen ChatGPT uses relevant personal context, **Sources** may appear below the response. **Sources** can help you review information such as a past chat, saved memory, custom instruction, file, or connected email that contributed to personalization.\n\nSources may not show every factor that shaped a response. Memory Sources are not included when you share a conversation through a shared link.\n\nDepending on the source and available controls, you may be able to:\n\n* open or review the source\n* correct or delete a saved memory\n* delete a referenced chat\n* mark a source as relevant or not relevant\n* open a referenced file or email\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.59.26 AM\n\n...\n\n## Remove remembered information from its sources\n\nTo remove information saved as a memory, delete the saved memory and the chat where you first shared it. Also remove the information from any other sources where it appears:\n\n* the memory summary\n* saved memories\n* regular and archived chats\n* files in Library\n* connected apps\n\nIt can take time for deletion and Memory updates to propagate. OpenAI may retain logs of deleted saved memories for up to 30 days for safety and debugging purposes.\n\n# Reference chat history\n\nIf your settings include Reference chat history, turning it on lets ChatGPT use relevant information from past conversations to personalize future responses.\n\nUnlike an explicit saved memory, information derived from chat history can change as ChatGPT updates what is most useful to remember.\n\nIf you turn **Reference chat history** off, information remembered from past chats is scheduled for deletion from OpenAI systems within 30 days.\n\n...\n\nWorkspace owners and admins can make Use improved memory available to the default workspace role or eligible custom roles.\n\nThis feature is not covered under your BAA. PHI should not be entered when using this feature.\n\nMembers who choose to use improved memory can use Project-only memory to keep memory context limited to a specific project. Chats can reference other conversations in the same project, but they cannot reference conversations outside the project, and chats outside the project cannot reference conversations in it. Project-only memory changes where context can be referenced; it does not change the BAA guidance in this section.\n\nFor setup and availability requirements, see: [Projects in ChatGPT](https://help.openai.com/articles/10169521) .\n\nBefore enabling improved memory, workspace owners and admins should review who will receive access and tell affected members about this restriction.\n\n...\n\nChatGPT](https://help.openai.com/articles/7730893) .\n\n# FAQ\n\n## Does the memory summary include everything ChatGPT remembers?\n\nNo. The summary is a high-level view and may omit details that are less relevant, unsuitable for the summary, or derived from sources that are not displayed individually.\n\n## Is memory different from custom instructions?\n\nYes. Custom instructions are direct guidance that you provide about what ChatGPT should know and how it should respond. Memory can use relevant information that develops across conversations and other available sources.\n\nFor more information about custom instructions, see: [ChatGPT Custom Instructions](https://help.openai.com/articles/8096356) .\n\n## Can ChatGPT remember my name or account identity?\n\nChatGPT can remember a name that you provide. When **Reference chat history** is enabled, ChatGPT may also use the account name already shown in the product when that information is relevant.\n\n## Does ChatGPT search my history for every response?\n\nNo."]},{"source_id":"gs8ThlhKsIU7P7VVjmS2J","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xPtoNdob378","title":"How to Use the New ChatGPT Memory Feature ...","publish_date":null,"excerpts":["How to Use the New ChatGPT Memory Feature ...\n... 답변 출처를 확인하는 법, 그리고 민감 정보를 안전하게 다루는 팁까지 5 ... ChatGPT #챗지피티메모리 #AI활용법 #생성형AI."]},{"source_id":"VJ5NBzCea5xbpMrO8IDBu","url":"https://www.ai-toolbox.co/chatgpt-management-and-productivity/how-to-manage-chatgpt-memory-2026","title":"How to Manage ChatGPT Memory: View, Edit, Delete (2026)","publish_date":"2026-05-30","excerpts":["OpenAI's stated mitigation is the Sources panel described in the next section, which names the specific memory or chat behind a given answer."]},{"source_id":"iHGUSu9xnBgmEBAFgl1Y3","url":"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8590148-memory-and-controls-faq","title":"Memory in ChatGPT | OpenAI Help Center","publish_date":null,"excerpts":["Turning off **Memory** or personalization does not disable limited safety and security uses of context in rare, high-risk situations. Those uses are separate from personalization controls.\n\n# Review what ChatGPT remembers\n\n## Memory summary\n\nThe memory summary is a high-level view of information that ChatGPT may use to personalize responses. It does not necessarily include every detail or source that Memory can reference.\n\nYou can also ask ChatGPT what it remembers about you.\n\nWhen the memory summary is available, you can:\n\n* Enter a correction in the text field.\n* Highlight text and provide a correction.\n* Select Don't mention this again when that option is available.\n* Select **Delete and turn off memory** from the more options menu (•••).\n\nDon't mention this again reduces future references to the information. It does not delete the original source.\n\n**Delete and turn off memory** deletes the remembered information shown in the summary and turns **Memory** off.\nIt does not delete past chats.\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.58.35 AM\n\n## Sources\n\nWhen ChatGPT uses relevant personal context, **Sources** may appear below the response. **Sources** can help you review information such as a past chat, saved memory, custom instruction, file, or connected email that contributed to personalization.\n\nSources may not show every factor that shaped a response. Memory Sources are not included when you share a conversation through a shared link.\n\nDepending on the source and available controls, you may be able to:\n\n* open or review the source\n* correct or delete a saved memory\n* delete a referenced chat\n* mark a source as relevant or not relevant\n* open a referenced file or email\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.59.26 AM\n\n# Correct or remove remembered information\n\n## Correct information\n\nYou can tell ChatGPT that remembered information is incorrect or outdated. You can also edit the memory summary or a saved memory when those controls are available.\n\n...\n\nMembers who choose to use improved memory can use Project-only memory to keep memory context limited to a specific project. Chats can reference other conversations in the same project, but they cannot reference conversations outside the project, and chats outside the project cannot reference conversations in it. Project-only memory changes where context can be referenced; it does not change the BAA guidance in this section.\n\nFor setup and availability requirements, see: [Projects in ChatGPT](https://help.openai.com/articles/10169521) .\n\nBefore enabling improved memory, workspace owners and admins should review who will receive access and tell affected members about this restriction. If a memory setting is unavailable in an Enterprise workspace, contact your workspace admin.\n\nFor the current list of functionality covered and not covered under the BAA, see: [HIPAA Eligible Products and Functionality](https://help.openai.com/articles/20001069) .\n\n# Memory in temporary chat\n\n...\n\n## Is memory different from custom instructions?\n\nYes. Custom instructions are direct guidance that you provide about what ChatGPT should know and how it should respond. Memory can use relevant information that develops across conversations and other available sources.\n\nFor more information about custom instructions, see: [ChatGPT Custom Instructions](https://help.openai.com/articles/8096356) .\n\n## Can ChatGPT remember my name or account identity?\n\nChatGPT can remember a name that you provide. When **Reference chat history** is enabled, ChatGPT may also use the account name already shown in the product when that information is relevant.\n\n## Does ChatGPT search my history for every response?\n\nNo. ChatGPT looks for relevant context when it is likely to improve a response.\n\n## Can memory personalize web searches?\n\nYes. When Memory is enabled, ChatGPT may use relevant details to formulate a more useful search query."]},{"source_id":"C9rp6XVWk9LZXpsCetjv1","url":"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10303002-how-does-memory-use-pastconversations","title":"Memory in ChatGPT | OpenAI Help Center","publish_date":null,"excerpts":["Turning off **Memory** or personalization does not disable limited safety and security uses of context in rare, high-risk situations. Those uses are separate from personalization controls.\n\n# Review what ChatGPT remembers\n\n## Memory summary\n\nThe memory summary is a high-level view of information that ChatGPT may use to personalize responses. It does not necessarily include every detail or source that Memory can reference.\n\nYou can also ask ChatGPT what it remembers about you.\n\nWhen the memory summary is available, you can:\n\n* Enter a correction in the text field.\n* Highlight text and provide a correction.\n* Select Don't mention this again when that option is available.\n* Select **Delete and turn off memory** from the more options menu (•••).\n\nDon't mention this again reduces future references to the information. It does not delete the original source.\n\n**Delete and turn off memory** deletes the remembered information shown in the summary and turns **Memory** off.\nIt does not delete past chats.\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.58.35 AM\n\n## Sources\n\nWhen ChatGPT uses relevant personal context, **Sources** may appear below the response. **Sources** can help you review information such as a past chat, saved memory, custom instruction, file, or connected email that contributed to personalization.\n\nSources may not show every factor that shaped a response. Memory Sources are not included when you share a conversation through a shared link.\n\nDepending on the source and available controls, you may be able to:\n\n* open or review the source\n* correct or delete a saved memory\n* delete a referenced chat\n* mark a source as relevant or not relevant\n* open a referenced file or email\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.59.26 AM\n\n# Correct or remove remembered information\n\n## Correct information\n\nYou can tell ChatGPT that remembered information is incorrect or outdated. You can also edit the memory summary or a saved memory when those controls are available.\n\n...\n\nMembers who choose to use improved memory can use Project-only memory to keep memory context limited to a specific project. Chats can reference other conversations in the same project, but they cannot reference conversations outside the project, and chats outside the project cannot reference conversations in it. Project-only memory changes where context can be referenced; it does not change the BAA guidance in this section.\n\nFor setup and availability requirements, see: [Projects in ChatGPT](https://help.openai.com/articles/10169521) .\n\nBefore enabling improved memory, workspace owners and admins should review who will receive access and tell affected members about this restriction. If a memory setting is unavailable in an Enterprise workspace, contact your workspace admin.\n\nFor the current list of functionality covered and not covered under the BAA, see: [HIPAA Eligible Products and Functionality](https://help.openai.com/articles/20001069) .\n\n# Memory in temporary chat\n\n...\n\n## Is memory different from custom instructions?\n\nYes. Custom instructions are direct guidance that you provide about what ChatGPT should know and how it should respond. Memory can use relevant information that develops across conversations and other available sources.\n\nFor more information about custom instructions, see: [ChatGPT Custom Instructions](https://help.openai.com/articles/8096356) .\n\n## Can ChatGPT remember my name or account identity?\n\nChatGPT can remember a name that you provide. When **Reference chat history** is enabled, ChatGPT may also use the account name already shown in the product when that information is relevant.\n\n## Does ChatGPT search my history for every response?\n\nNo. ChatGPT looks for relevant context when it is likely to improve a response.\n\n## Can memory personalize web searches?\n\nYes. When Memory is enabled, ChatGPT may use relevant details to formulate a more useful search query."]},{"source_id":"dzPO1usf94eVTJtIl6wNo","url":"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8590148","title":"Memory in ChatGPT | OpenAI Help Center","publish_date":null,"excerpts":["Turning off **Memory** or personalization does not disable limited safety and security uses of context in rare, high-risk situations. Those uses are separate from personalization controls.\n\n# Review what ChatGPT remembers\n\n## Memory summary\n\nThe memory summary is a high-level view of information that ChatGPT may use to personalize responses. It does not necessarily include every detail or source that Memory can reference.\n\nYou can also ask ChatGPT what it remembers about you.\n\nWhen the memory summary is available, you can:\n\n* Enter a correction in the text field.\n* Highlight text and provide a correction.\n* Select Don't mention this again when that option is available.\n* Select **Delete and turn off memory** from the more options menu (•••).\n\nDon't mention this again reduces future references to the information. It does not delete the original source.\n\n**Delete and turn off memory** deletes the remembered information shown in the summary and turns **Memory** off.\nIt does not delete past chats.\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.58.35 AM\n\n## Sources\n\nWhen ChatGPT uses\n\n...\n\nMembers who choose to use improved memory can use Project-only memory to keep memory context limited to a specific project. Chats can reference other conversations in the same project, but they cannot reference conversations outside the project, and chats outside the project cannot reference conversations in it. Project-only memory changes where context can be referenced; it does not change the BAA guidance in this section.\n\nFor setup and availability requirements, see: [Projects in ChatGPT](https://help.openai.com/articles/10169521) .\n\nBefore enabling improved memory, workspace owners and admins should review who will receive access and tell affected members about this restriction. If a memory setting is unavailable in an Enterprise workspace, contact your workspace admin.\n\nFor the current list of functionality covered and not covered under the BAA, see: [HIPAA Eligible Products and Functionality](https://help.openai.com/articles/20001069) .\n\n# Memory in temporary chat\n\n...\n\n## Is memory different from custom instructions?\n\nYes. Custom instructions are direct guidance that you provide about what ChatGPT should know and how it should respond. Memory can use relevant information that develops across conversations and other available sources.\n\nFor more information about custom instructions, see: [ChatGPT Custom Instructions](https://help.openai.com/articles/8096356) .\n\n## Can ChatGPT remember my name or account identity?\n\nChatGPT can remember a name that you provide. When **Reference chat history** is enabled, ChatGPT may also use the account name already shown in the product when that information is relevant.\n\n## Does ChatGPT search my history for every response?\n\nNo. ChatGPT looks for relevant context when it is likely to improve a response.\n\n## Can memory personalize web searches?\n\nYes. When Memory is enabled, ChatGPT may use relevant details to formulate a more useful search query."]},{"source_id":"BdVWE9syhYcstCcyhmtN5","url":"https://help.openai.com/ko-kr/articles/8590148-memory-in-chatgpt","title":"ChatGPT의 메모리","publish_date":null,"excerpts":["[OpenAI](https://help.openai.com/ko-kr)\n\n1. [All Collections](https://help.openai.com/ko-kr)\n2. [ChatGPT](https://help.openai.com/ko-kr/collections/3742473-chatgpt)\n3. [메모리](https://help.openai.com/ko-kr/collections/8471548-memory)\n4. ChatGPT의 메모리\n\n이 페이지는 기계 번역되었습니다. [영어 원문 보기](https://help.openai.com/resources/translation-view-redirect?articleId=8590148&routeLanguage=ko-kr&redirectTo=%2Fen%2Farticles%2F8590148-memory-in-chatgpt)\n\n번역 피드백 남기기\n\n# ChatGPT의 메모리\n\nChatGPT가 메모리를 사용해 응답을 개인화하는 방식과 기억된 정보를 검토, 변경 또는 삭제하는 방법을 알아보세요.\n\n마지막 수정: 18 days ago\n\n# 개요\n\n메모리가 활성화되면 ChatGPT가 채팅과 사용 가능한 다른 출처에서 관련된 선호 사항과 세부 정보를 기억할 수 있습니다. 이를 통해 이전에 중단한 지점부터 이어서 진행하고 같은 내용을 반복하는 시간을 줄일 수 있습니다.\n\n메모리 기능과 제어 항목은 요금제, 지역, 플랫폼 및 워크스페이스 설정에 따라 다를 수 있습니다. 여기에 설명된 설정이 표시되지 않는다면 아직 계정에서 사용할 수 없는 기능일 수 있습니다.\n\n요금제와 지역에 따라 다음 출처가 포함될 수 있습니다.\n\n* 이전 채팅\n* 저장된 메모리\n* 맞춤 지침\n* 라이브러리의 파일\n* Gmail과 같은 연결된 앱의 콘텐츠\n\n메모리가 모든 대화의 모든 세부 정보를 기억하지는 않습니다. ChatGPT는 사용 가능한 정보 중 응답과 관련된 정보를 판단하며, 맥락이 바뀌면 메모리도 변경될 수 있습니다.\n\n# 메모리 설정 관리\n\n계정에서 사용할 수 있는 **메모리** 제어 기능을 검토하려면 다음 단계를 따르세요.\n\n1. **설정** 을 엽니다.\n2. **개인화** 를 선택합니다.\n3. **메모리** 를 선택합니다.\n사용 중인 메모리 환경에 따라 **메모리** , **저장된 메모리 참조** , **채팅 기록 참조** , **메모리 요약** , **관리** 또는 **저장된 메모리** 등의 제어 기능을 사용할 수 있습니다.\n\n연결된 청소년 계정의 경우 부모나 보호자가 [자녀 보호](https://help.openai.com/articles/12315553) 를 통해 지원되는 메모리 제어 기능을 관리할 수 있습니다.\n\n**메모리** 를 꺼도 이전 채팅은 삭제되지 않습니다. 나중에 **메모리** 를 켜면 ChatGPT가 기록에 남아 있는 채팅에서 새로운 정보를 기억할 수 있습니다.\n\n**메모리** 또는 개인화를 꺼도 드물게 발생하는 고위험 상황에서 맥락을 제한적으로 활용하는 안전 및 보안 기능은 비활성화되지 않습니다. 이러한 활용은 개인화 제어와 별개입니다.\n\n# ChatGPT가 기억하는 내용 검토\n\n## 메모리 요약\n\n메모리 요약은 ChatGPT가 응답 개인화에 사용할 수 있는 정보를 개괄적으로 보여 줍니다. 메모리가 참조할 수 있는 모든 세부 정보나 출처가 반드시 포함되는 것은 아닙니다.\n\nChatGPT에 나에 대해 무엇을 기억하는지 물어볼 수도 있습니다.\n\n메모리 요약을 사용할 수 있는 경우 다음 작업을 할 수 있습니다.\n\n* 텍스트 필드에 수정 내용을 입력합니다.\n* 텍스트를 강조 표시하고 수정 내용을 제공합니다.\n* 옵션을 사용할 수 있다면 다시 언급하지 않기를 선택합니다.\n* 더보기 옵션 메뉴(•••)에서 **삭제하고 메모리 끄기** 를 선택합니다.\n\n다시 언급하지 않기를 선택하면 향후 해당 정보가 참조되는 빈도가 줄어듭니다. 원래 출처가 삭제되는 것은 아닙니다.\n\n**삭제하고 메모리 끄기** 를 선택하면 요약에 표시된 기억된 정보가 삭제되고 **메모리** 가 꺼집니다. 이전 채팅은 삭제되지 않습니다.\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.58.35 AM\n\n## 출처\n\n...\n\nChatGPT에 저장된 메모리를 잊도록 요청하거나 메모리 설정에서 직접 삭제할 수 있습니다. 저장된 메모리를 삭제하면 향후 개인화에 사용되지 않지만, 이전 대화에서 해당 정보가 언급된 부분은 삭제되지 않습니다.\n\n요금제와 플랫폼에 따라 저장된 메모리 제어 기능에 검색, 정렬, 자동 우선순위 지정 및 버전 기록이 포함될 수도 있습니다.\n\n# 향상된 메모리와 기존 저장된 메모리\n\n향상된 메모리는 관련 맥락을 더 폭넓게 요약하여 지속적으로 업데이트합니다. 기존 저장된 메모리는 개별 메모리 항목을 보다 명시적인 목록으로 관리합니다.\n\n옵션이 제공되는 경우 다음과 같이 환경을 전환할 수 있습니다.\n\n1. **설정** 을 엽니다.\n2. **개인화** 를 선택합니다.\n3. **메모리** 를 선택합니다.\n4. 기존 환경을 사용하려면 **저장된 메모리** 를 선택하고, 향상된 **메모리** 로 돌아가려면 **향상된 메모리 사용해 보기** 를 선택합니다.\n\n메모리 환경을 변경해도 채팅 기록은 삭제되지 않습니다.\n\n# 규제 대상 워크스페이스의 향상된 메모리\n\n향상된 메모리는 이전 채팅의 맥락을 활용하여 메모리를 최신 상태로 유지할 수 있습니다. 이는 일반적인 메모리 및 기존 저장된 메모리 시스템과는 별개의 기능입니다.\n\n의료 서비스용 ChatGPT와 규제 대상 워크스페이스가 적용된 ChatGPT Enterprise에서는 향상된 메모리가 기본적으로 비활성화되어 있습니다. 워크스페이스 소유자와 관리자는 기본 워크스페이스 역할이나 자격 요건을 충족하는 맞춤 역할에서 향상된 메모리 사용 기능을 이용할 수 있도록 설정할 수 있습니다.\n\n이 기능은 BAA의 적용 대상이 아닙니다. 이 기능을 사용할 때는 PHI를 입력하지 마세요."]},{"source_id":"O_B9lY11FvAUA9HX5lWLX","url":"https://www.mindstudio.ai/blog/gpt-55-instant-memory-source-citations-hidden-ui-changes","title":"GPT-5.5 Instant Memory Now Shows Which Saved Memory It Used — And 4 Other Hidden UI Changes | MindStudio","publish_date":"2026-05-09","excerpts":["GPT-5.5 Instant something that touches on your saved memories — say, “tell me about myself” or any question where personal context is relevant — the response now includes a **Sources** section underneath. That section links to the specific saved memory the model referenced.\n\nThis sounds minor. It isn’t.\n\n## Plans first. _Then code._\n\nPROJECT YOUR APP\n\nSCREENS 12\n\nDB TABLES 6\n\nBUILT BY REMY\n\n1280 px · TYP.\n\nyourapp.msagent.ai\n\nA · UI · FRONT END\n\nRemy writes the spec, manages the build, and ships the app.\n\nRemy The world's most powerful product manager agent [Try Remy today](https://goremy.ai/?utm_source=blog&utm_medium=interstitial&utm_campaign=remy-blog)\n\nThe core problem with opaque memory systems is that errors compound silently. If ChatGPT stored an incorrect fact about you — your job title, a preference, a project you’re no longer working on — and you didn’t know it was being used, every subsequent response would quietly inherit that error.\n\n...\n\n## Five Changes, Walked Through\n\n### 1\\. Memory now cites its sources\n\nAs described above: ask something personal, look for the Sources section, click through to see which saved memory was used. The three-dot menu on that memory gives you “make a correction.” Use it.\n\nThe practical workflow: after any response that feels slightly off in its personalization, check the sources. If the cited memory is stale or wrong, correct it immediately. This is much faster than the old approach of periodically auditing your full memory list.\n\nNow you have a feedback loop for memory quality that didn’t exist before.\n\n### 2\\. Search results now append FAQ sections\n\nThis one showed up in team testing and is easy to miss because it looks like a formatting choice rather than a feature. When GPT-5.5 Instant handles a search-style query — “best games of 2025,” “how to set up X,” anything with a research flavor — the response now ends with a FAQ section that addresses likely follow-up questions.\n\n...\n\nplace.** Citations only help if the underlying memories are accurate. If ChatGPT stored something wrong during a past conversation, the citation feature will surface that wrong memory — which is actually good, because now you can see and fix it. But don’t expect citations to fix bad data; they just make bad data visible.\n\n## Other agents ship a demo. Remy ships an app.\n\nUI\n\nReact + Tailwind ✓ LIVE\n\nAPI\n\nREST · typed contracts ✓ LIVE\n\nDATABASE\n\nreal SQL, not mocked ✓ LIVE\n\nAUTH\n\nroles · sessions · tokens ✓ LIVE\n\nDEPLOY\n\ngit-backed, live URL ✓ LIVE\n\nReal backend. Real database. Real auth. Real plumbing. Remy has it all.\n\nRemy The world's most powerful product manager agent [Try Remy today](https://goremy.ai/?utm_source=blog&utm_medium=interstitial&utm_campaign=remy-blog)\n\n**Memory citation doesn’t appear on every response.** It only shows up when the model actually drew on a saved memory. If your query doesn’t trigger memory retrieval, you won’t see a Sources section.\n\n...\n\nLLMs & Models GPT & OpenAI Productivity](https://www.mindstudio.ai/blog/gpt-5) [July 22, 2026 ### The Context Sandwich: The Prompting Method That Gets Better AI Results The Context Sandwich structures prompts with who you are, the task, and what good looks like. Learn how to use it for better AI outputs. Prompt Engineering GPT & OpenAI Productivity](https://www.mindstudio.ai/blog/context-sandwich-prompting-method-better-ai-results)"]},{"source_id":"RFMslxCTrSY3w8walTktD","url":"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10303002-how-does-memory-use-past-conversations","title":"Memory FAQ | OpenAI Help Center","publish_date":null,"excerpts":["Turning off **Memory** or personalization does not disable limited safety and security uses of context in rare, high-risk situations. Those uses are separate from personalization controls.\n\n# Review what ChatGPT remembers\n\n## Memory summary\n\nThe memory summary is a high-level view of information that ChatGPT may use to personalize responses. It does not necessarily include every detail or source that Memory can reference.\n\nYou can also ask ChatGPT what it remembers about you.\n\nWhen the memory summary is available, you can:\n\n* Enter a correction in the text field.\n* Highlight text and provide a correction.\n* Select Don't mention this again when that option is available.\n* Select **Delete and turn off memory** from the more options menu (•••).\n\nDon't mention this again reduces future references to the information. It does not delete the original source.\n\n**Delete and turn off memory** deletes the remembered information shown in the summary and turns **Memory** off.\n\n...\n\nMembers who choose to use improved memory can use Project-only memory to keep memory context limited to a specific project. Chats can reference other conversations in the same project, but they cannot reference conversations outside the project, and chats outside the project cannot reference conversations in it. Project-only memory changes where context can be referenced; it does not change the BAA guidance in this section.\n\nFor setup and availability requirements, see: [Projects in ChatGPT](https://help.openai.com/articles/10169521) .\n\nBefore enabling improved memory, workspace owners and admins should review who will receive access and tell affected members about this restriction. If a memory setting is unavailable in an Enterprise workspace, contact your workspace admin.\n\nFor the current list of functionality covered and not covered under the BAA, see: [HIPAA Eligible Products and Functionality](https://help.openai.com/articles/20001069) .\n\n# Memory in temporary chat\n\n...\n\n## Is memory different from custom instructions?\n\nYes. Custom instructions are direct guidance that you provide about what ChatGPT should know and how it should respond. Memory can use relevant information that develops across conversations and other available sources.\n\nFor more information about custom instructions, see: [ChatGPT Custom Instructions](https://help.openai.com/articles/8096356) .\n\n## Can ChatGPT remember my name or account identity?\n\nChatGPT can remember a name that you provide. When **Reference chat history** is enabled, ChatGPT may also use the account name already shown in the product when that information is relevant.\n\n## Does ChatGPT search my history for every response?\n\nNo. ChatGPT looks for relevant context when it is likely to improve a response.\n\n## Can memory personalize web searches?\n\nYes. When Memory is enabled, ChatGPT may use relevant details to formulate a more useful search query."]},{"source_id":"hDL5L1Hm9xrh2n_HG95n6","url":"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8590148-memory-faq%C3%AF%C2%BF%C2%BC%5b10%5d","title":"Memory FAQ | OpenAI Help Center","publish_date":null,"excerpts":["You can see what sources were used to personalize a response such as custom instructions, past chats, files, and memories by tapping the book icon below the response.  \n  \nTapping on a memory in sources will open an explanation on why that memory was used to personalize a response.  \n  \nYou can also make a correction by selecting the 3 dot menu (•••).  \n  \nSources are designed to make memory easier to understand and control, though they may not show every factor or source that shaped a response. Memory sources are not included in chats you share.\n\nScreenshot 2026-06-04 at 8.59.26 AM\n\n# How we've improved upon the previous saved memories experience\n\nThe previous saved memories system often became stale and relied on users to manually manage updates. Memories could also contradict one another, such as “I’m training for a marathon” and “I sprained my ankle,” which made personalization less accurate."]}]}[0m
[2mThinking: I realize the sources are actually shown via a book icon below the response, not a labeled button as I assumed - I must have missed it among the icons for copy, rate response, read aloud, and regenerate, since none of their accessibility labels mentioned a book icon.

This absence could itself be meaningful: maybe the book icon only appears conditionally when sources exist, so with memory off, no icon appearing at all would be the signal confirming no memory section. I should track whether a book icon appears across all three turns rather than assuming its absence means failure. I'll proceed with checking before and after each of the three messages, noting the presence or absence of a source panel each time, and the third question about studio recommendations is likely the clearest test since it would reveal if past memory is being referenced.

